      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe NPU V4 Indexer pool allocates the base CUDA-format packed cache as well as separate native K and scale buffers. NPU writes, PD registration and HiCache use the native buffers; the packed allocation is never updated.\n\nWith 65,536 compressed slots and four Indexer layers, removing it reduces measured pool allocations from 65.67 MiB to 32.54 MiB when the FP4 indexer option is off.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Skip the unused packed allocation.\n- Expose the native buffers as shared-storage byte views through `contiguous_page_row_buffers()`.\n- Reject the packed-only accessor explicitly instead of returning unused storage.\n- Update the comments describing the pool layout.\n\nNative buffer shapes, dtypes and write operations are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nReused the original and patched source methods in an isolated harness with generic KVCache setup scaffolded:\n\n- 8 NPU cases passed: sizes 0/64/1024/65536, FP4 option off/on, four layers, head dimension 128, native page size 64 and global page size 256.\n- Native K/scale writes and readback match exactly before and after. PD pointer/length metadata and HiCache region selection refer to the native buffers. Page-row views share storage and pass host/device round-trip checks.\n- 16 CPU cases passed, additionally checking the arch35 FP8/FP32 layout. No arch35 hardware run was performed.\n\nThese are pool-level checks, not full-model accuracy or cross-host PD tests.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nMeasured `torch.npu.memory_allocated()` deltas for pool construction at 65,536 slots and four layers:\n\n| FP4 option | Before | After | Saved |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Off | 68,855,808 bytes | 34,115,584 bytes | 33.13 MiB |\n| On | 52,013,056 bytes | 34,115,584 bytes | 17.07 MiB |\n\nThe option changes the old packed allocation, not the native NPU buffers. These savings apply to the Indexer pool, not total model memory. Throughput was not benchmarked.\n\n![NPU Indexer validation](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/AkiYangDev/sglang@5226dcc9e489c50a91b0ae9608adb2177c7c6855/validation.png)\n\n[Raw NPU results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/5226dcc9e489c50a91b0ae9608adb2177c7c6855/RESULT_npu.json) · [CPU results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/5226dcc9e489c50a91b0ae9608adb2177c7c6855/RESULT_cpu.json)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting and applicable lint checks passed. Two hooks requiring `python3` on Windows were run directly with the installed Python.\n- [x] NPU pool correctness and allocation checks completed.\n- [ ] Full-model accuracy, throughput and cross-host PD validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41199042620](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41199042620)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41199042498](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41199042498)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41199042536](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41199042536)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
